  "issues": "No errors or warnings before probe completion in all six engine logs; stdout/stderr added no unmatched issue messages. Shutdown resource/material/RID errors retained separately in original logs.",
  "excluded_pilot": "One minigun + three shotgun cards produced only 98 bullets/12s and is excluded. Final heavy case uses three of each card.",
  "limitations": [
    "Both workloads are more consistent with host-side work, scheduling or synchronization limits than viewport GPU saturation: process-loop intervals are much longer than the separately measured viewport GPU work. This is an inference, not an exclusive CPU attribution.",
    "GPU work and CPU work overlap, timestamps can lag, and process-loop wall time includes all waits. Do not subtract GPU time from loop time to manufacture total CPU time. Viewport timings do not include all presentation/compositor cost.",
    "Explosion runs become substantially faster during the measure window. Fixed warmup does not produce a stationary workload: startup/cache settling, changes in bot activity, effect budgets, and terrain depletion can all contribute. Early-versus-late windows are retained instead of declaring one cause.",
    "The 3x minigun + 3x shotgun bullet case retains the authored projectile cap and physics firing cadence; it is not an unlimited bullet generator.",
    "Explosion mode combines four bots with 40/s nominal simulated-time wall spray. ev_explosions counts bullet collisions only; blast_calls/full/cheap include manual spray. Full/cheap are branch counters, not simultaneously visible effect counts.",
    "Adaptive governor is disabled at quality 1, with original per-frame effect/time caps retained. Per-frame budgets can change the realized full/cheap workload as frame cadence changes.",
    "Process callbacks are sampled strictly inside the observed measure phase; boundary intervals, initial startup and final report printing are excluded. This is offscreen rendering, not an onscreen presentation-latency test.",
    "Fixed seed does not guarantee identical trajectories in a timing-dependent simulation. Event totals, destruction and full/cheap mix must accompany timing comparisons.",
    "Shutdown errors are retained separately and do not fall inside recorded intervals. No scene/source/PCK fixes are included in this measurement task."
  ],
  "portable_launcher_difference": "Only the default output directory changed from beside the script to C:/dev/warp-bench/godot-stress-<timestamp>; probe bytes are unchanged."
}